findings.citation_text:
4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) back prep table - bottom shelf and inside drawer (food splash/debris);
B) large prep cooler - general surfaces and handles (splash/grimy buildup);
C) fridge - bottom inside (food splash);
D) fryer - sides (grease/food debris);
E) wok grill - ledge underneath and drip trays (grease/food debris);
F) small table holding spices at wok grill (splash/food debris);
G) small grill - sides and drip tray (grease buildup);   and
H) table holding small grill (grease/food debris).
Clean the aforementioned items.
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) prep coolers - all general surfaces (sticky buildup); 
B) walkin cooler fan cover (dust/mold buildup);
C) 2 door freezer - bottom inside (splash/crumbs);  
D) cooking area - sides, bottom, and underneath all equipment (grease/food debris);   and
E) can opener drawer (splash). 

Clean general surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - Surfaces were soiled with general buildup of food crumbs/splash and/or debris in the following areas:
A) large prep cooler handles and doors;
B) table between fryers and wok grill; 
C) sides and underneath surfaces of cooking equipment;  and
D) inside freezers

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed, and maintain them clean.
